            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "cookiesncream"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I had an urge for a Tim Horton's Iced cappuccino one day and found this recipe. I think it's awsome, but a litte tip of variation for iced cap lovers: Instead of putting the coffee and milk mixture in a glass of ice, blend it in with the ice in a blender, if you have an ice breaker. The taste and texture are almost like the one at Tim Hortons. Try it, you'll get hooked and won't have to spend two dollars at Timmy's every morning."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "RF369"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I did a new variation of this recipe with great results: decaf coffee crystals, sugar substitute and fat free french vanilla dairy creamer--enjoy, I did.",
            "datePublished": "2005-08-03T11:38:48.187Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "liz"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have been using this recipe for a long time (2016) It’s so simple. I add all ingredients to a 12oz mason jar with a lid. Makes for easy clean up. Sometimes I like to add 1 to 1 1/2tsps of brown sugar, 1/2 tsp Ceylon cinnamon, &amp; 1 tsp pure vanilla extract. The taste is like a cinnamon dolce. The variety is endless with homemade or store bought coffee syrups.",
            "datePublished": "2025-07-28T17:35:07.906Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jana"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Wow! I was sceptical that it would have the same quality taste as shop bought iced coffee, but i am pleasantly surprised!! 10/10. This just became my favourite go to Summer drink. Absolutely yummy!! I altered mine a bit after reading comments, added another tsp of sugar and 1tsp of vanilla essence. I used 1 tsp douwe egberts strong instant coffee and 1 tsp ricoffy chicory instant coffee. And i used a milk frother whisk to make it creamy instead of shaking. Thank you so much for this recipe! Absolutely delicious ♥️😋👌🏻",
            "datePublished": "2026-01-10T22:14:26.865Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Courtney Hope VanderKlip"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is so yummy! I made a few changes for my own tastes. I used unsweetened almond milk, added a couple table spoons of heavy cream and shook that up, added a tablespoon on sweet vanilla creamer, cinnamon on top and vanilla extract. DELICIOUS. I can’t wait to try different flavors! I used nestle Classico for the instant coffee.",
            "datePublished": "2021-07-15T13:44:12.557Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Howayda Negm"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very tasty .. I just added one teaspoon of vanilla ice cream and omitted the sugar and put everything in elec. mixer instead of shaking a jar",
            "datePublished": "2015-08-12T07:13:12.710Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
